    "g7": {
      "x": 1990,
      "y": 12904,
      "w": 400,
      "fill": "blue",
      "text": "Landing rationale\n\nGoal: waitlist before launch (no TestFlight invite yet). Platform pick (iPhone / Android) on the form measures Android demand. One email field, shown twice (hero + end). Inline error, success replaces the form.\nVI first, EN toggle in the nav. Copy is short and plain, same voice as the app.\nFeature tour: tabs + swipeable phone with the real screens, autoplays every 6 s until the user touches it.\nPitch = speed: three steps, and a live hold-to-unlock demo. The car changes only after the fake confirm, same rule as the app.\nHonest block before the FAQ: password goes only to Honda, one phone at a time, not made by Honda.\nNo Honda logo anywhere. Footer says not affiliated.\nHero: big red Civic RS cycles locked, unlocked, engine on every 3.4 s (HUD chips follow; the pills below pick a state and stop the loop; Reduce Motion stops autoplay).\nFeatures list everything planned; mark launch-later ones with the .soon tag when the launch scope is set.\nVI copy follows the app dictionary: khóa, điều hòa, nổ máy, nhấn giữ. No time promise: Honda can take ~20 s to answer.\nRegistered state (hero): check draws in, email + platform echoed, optional 2-question survey (car model, most wanted features) to size demand, then a share link. The end-of-page form keeps a one-line success.\nOpen: email provider for the list, privacy page, domain."
    },
    "t8": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 9760,
      "text": "States: loading, offline, empty, errors, toasts",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 6090
    },
    "g6": {
      "x": 6170,
      "y": 10060,
      "w": 380,
      "fill": "yellow",
      "text": "State rules\n\nLoading: skeleton in the real layout, never a spinner page. Cached data shows at once with its age; skeleton only on very first load.\nOffline vs asleep: no internet = grey banner, commands disabled with reason. Car asleep = amber line, commands still allowed (they queue + wake).\nSigned out elsewhere: Honda allows one phone. Explain, keep the car picture, one button to sign in again.\nPackage expired: read-only data stays, remote actions replaced by one renew link.\nToast = result of something you just did (3 s, top, swipe up). Banner = ongoing condition (stays until fixed). Errors on a form = inline under the field, not a toast."
    },
    "g5": {
      "x": 3760,
      "y": 5672,
      "w": 380,
      "fill": "green",
      "text": "Onboarding rationale\n\nGoal: first launch to unlocking the car in under 60 s.\n3 intro slides max, skippable. Then only what the API needs: region, phone + password, SMS code.\nStep 4 is the honest part: Honda binds an account to one phone. Signing in here signs the official app out. Say it before the SMS, not after.\nStep 6 is the reward: the car appears in its real color (from /car/image) with plate. Feels like a key handover.\nStep 7 lets the user pick body shape (pre-selected from the API model), style (shaded / line / Honda photo) and paint. Skippable.\nStep 8 groups Face ID, notifications and Siri on one screen, each skippable. No permission prompt without a reason line.\nProgress bar: 4 segments for sign-in steps only. Intro slides use dots."
    },
    "g4": {
      "x": 1410,
      "y": 8616,
      "w": 380,
      "fill": "orange",
      "text": "Account, multi-car, sharing\n\nSign in once; token in Keychain, Face ID to reopen. Password goes only to Honda.\nMulti-car: name on Home is the switcher. Swipe the car image left/right to change car. Widgets and Siri take a car (\"Lock the City\"); default = last used.\nShared cars show who shared them and only the actions you were given. Hidden actions are not shown greyed out.\nSharing: per-person permissions (location / lock / unlock / engine) + expiry. Unlock and engine need Face ID on the guest's device.\nDevices: every signed-in device is listed; sign out one or all.\n\nOpen question: if Honda's API has no guest users, sharing needs our own backend holding the owner's token. That is a security decision, not a UI one."
    },
    "g1": {
      "x": 1880,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 380,
      "fill": "blue",
      "text": "Gesture map\n\nTap = safe, reversible (Lock, open a screen).\nSwipe / scrub to choose, never tap-tap: swipe the car to change car or body shape; slide a knob for AC level and style; scrub a finger along the paint rail. Value changes live under the finger, haptic tick per stop, knob springs to the nearest stop on release. Taps and VoiceOver adjust (swipe up/down) still work.\nHold ~0.6 s = physical / risky (Unlock, Start engine). The pill fills under the thumb; release early cancels. Haptic: light tick at start, firm tap when armed.\nPull down on Home = wake the car + refresh. Not a reload: it sends a wake, then reads live data.\nSwipe left on a notification = delete. Edge-swipe = back.\nAll primary controls live in the bottom 40% of the screen."
    },
    "g2": {
      "x": 1880,
      "y": 520,
      "w": 380,
      "fill": "teal",
      "text": "Async command pattern\n\n1 Fire: button turns into its own progress ring at once. Haptic tick. No modal, no blocking.\n2 Accepted: one calm line says the car got it (\"Accepted · waiting for car\").\n3 Confirm: poll until the car reports the new state, then a success haptic and the headline changes.\nSlow / car asleep: amber \"Connection unstable — retrying\". Keep the last known state visible. Only after all retries: \"Couldn't reach car\" + Try again.\nThe UI is optimistic in motion, honest in words: the headline only changes when the car confirms."
    },
    "g3": {
      "x": 2960,
      "y": 3972,
      "w": 380,
      "fill": "purple",
      "text": "Siri flows\n\nEvery intent answers in one spoken sentence + a compact snippet, no app launch.\nRead intents (Is it locked? Where is it?) run at once.\nPhysical intents (Unlock, Start) ask \"Unlock your HR-V?\" — Siri confirmation is the voice version of long-press.\nLock needs no confirm.\nSlow car: Siri says \"Sent. I'll notify you when it's done.\" and a push confirms later."
    },
